cartoons are fun and sometimes they're  also super educational in some cases  they teach us about things that haven't  even happened yet whether it's the  Simpsons predicting the next president  or Zootopia anticipating the next  performance from a major star we can  look to cartoons for some clues about  where the world will take us next  so what fun surprising futuristic things  have cartoons accurately predicted about  our world stay tuned because we've  compiled a list of 10 of the coolest and  most accurate cartoon predictions in a  2017 episode of The Simpsons titled  serfs ins the cartoon most famously  known for predicting future events  managed to accurately predict a huge  Game of Thrones season 8 twist  insertions a game of Thrones themed  episode The Simpsons family stands on a  hill and watches as a dragon flies over  their town unleashing fire and burning  everything in its path the scene is  eerily similar to what happens in the  fifth episode of Game of Thrones season  8 which premiered two years after the  Simpsons prediction in the episode  titled the bells Daenerys and her forces  attack King's Landing leading to their  surrender but that isn't enough for  Danny she goes mad and lets her dragons  loose on the town the results look  almost identical to the Simpsons episode  complete with doom and gloom in a  village being burnt to the ground  Futurama has predicted a couple of  interesting things as well that are  becoming more and more mainstream like  their risk computers which are basically  just smartwatches but one of the most  interesting predictions appeared in the  1999 episode the series has landed while  at an amusement park on the moon the  Planet Express crew visits a video  arcade someone is playing skee-ball  while someone else is playing the  virtual skee-ball and mimicking the  motions of throwing an actual skee-ball  but the real punchline is the next  person they see who is playing virtual  virtual skee-ball basically they're just  sitting in a chair and doing nothing  with a cool headset on we can't deny  that this looks very similar to vr  gaming today even the headset bears a  remarkable resemblance to popular VR  headsets and as we're sitting in a chair  and doing nothing some of the VR that  exists today is just for a cool  experience and not so much for physical  gameplay so future Imus joke isn't so  far off from our reality The Simpsons  don't just accurately predict television  show twists they also know a thing or  two about movie studios all the way back  in 1998 The Simpsons aired an episode  called when you dish upon a star in the  episode a sign is showed on  thing that reads 20th century-fox a  division of the Walt Disney Company  almost 20 years later in 2017 Disney  officially announced a fifty two point  four billion dollar purchase that would  allow them to acquire twentieth  century-fox as well as national  geographic effects regional sports  networks and other assets funny enough  the Simpsons were just trying to poke  fun at their parent company Fox with  this one but later the Simpsons would  actually be streaming exclusively on  Disney plus we could chalk this guess up  to the showrunners understanding that  huge companies often merge and change  over time but it's still an incredibly  impressive Perdition to have made so far  in advance of the actual event but this  type of unbelievable prediction isn't  new for the Simpsons we have some even  crazier ones a little further down on  our list  Shakira put on an amazing halftime show  at the Super Bowl 54 but what's extra  cool about her performance is that it  bears a striking resemblance to another  of Shakira's performances but in that  one she was playing a gazelle in the  2016 animated film Zootopia Shakira  voices a pop superstar known as gazelle  when she performs for a crowd of animal  fans she's wearing a shimmery red outfit  complete with tassels for added movement  and flow Shakira's outfit at the  Superbowl was almost identical she even  had on the high red boots and both  versions of Shakira danced across the  stage with lots of movement and energy  so did Shakira actually take inspiration  directly from rizzuto Pia character it's  possible and Zootopia she's an icon that  brings animals together and she pretty  much did the same thing by performing on  the iconic Super Bowl stage if JLo had  also voiced the pop superstar on  Zootopia this Perdition would have been  even more epic Zootopia wasn't the only  animation to have a thing or two to say  about the Superbowl halftime shows and  the 2012 episode called Lisa goes gaga  The Simpsons displayed a very accurate  visual prediction of what Lady Gaga's  2017 Super Bowl halftime show would look  like in the episode Lady Gaga is  actually playing a Springfield concert  but she descends from the sky on wires  while wearing a harness and a glittery  silver outfit during her 2017 halftime  show Lady Gaga dropped down onto the  stage in a similar way and was wearing a  sparkly Versace number that was almost a  perfect match for the one who Simpsons  character wore and if that's not enough  she was flanked by drones in the sky  just as her character was during the  Springfield concert sure Lady Gaga is  known for some crazy stage antics and  fashion moments but she had never really  gone airborne or worn an outfit like  this before her Super Bowl performance  maybe the Simpsons knows Lady Gaga  better than she knows herself another  celebrity that the Simpson seems to know  pretty well is Donald Trump in an  episode that aired in 2000 called Bart  to the Future Lisa finds herself  becoming the next president of the  United States  she tells her team that they inherited  quite the budget crunch from President  Trump Trump would later go on to win the  presidency in real life in 2016 but the  prediction wasn't completely out of  nowhere back in 2000 Trump had already  revealed his intentions to one day run  for the presidency and the Simpsons  showrunners thought he would be a funny  choice for the episodes former president  but they never hoped he would actually  win a week after the election they  referenced their trump tradition in the  episodes chalkboard gag with a simple  line being write sucks The Simpsons had  a few more things to say about elections  in the 19th Treehouse of Horror episode  that aired in 2008 the show decided to  make some voter commentary connected to  the 2008 election when Homer goes into a  voting booth and chooses Barack Obama  the system automatically counts his vote  as being for John McCain while this  voting malfunction didn't occur during  the 2008 election a 2012 viral video  showed a voting booth in Pennsylvania  doing the same thing with Barack Obama  and Mitt Romney whenever the voter would  press Obama a checkmark would  automatically appear beside Romney's  name the voter repeatedly presses Obama  with the same results voting  malfunctions have been a topic of  conversation for many elections but the  Simpsons got this particular incident  almost exactly right with Obama being on  the losing side of both malfunctions  since there were a lot of reported  voting malfunctions and fraud in the  2016 election we imagine that this might  not be the only time the Simpsons voting  predictions will prove to be true in a  1999 episode titled the lesser of two  evils  Futurama managed to predict a pretty  surprising onstage mix-up in the episode  Zapp Brannigan is the judge of the Miss  Universe 3001 pageant when he has to  announce the winner he sees Leela off  stage and mistakenly says her name  instead of the one in the envelope  there's some confusion because she's not  even in the pageant but it's cleared up  when Zapp fixes his mistake and Gladys  Lennox is rightfully crowned the winner  Steve Harvey's major announcement  mistake during the 2015 Miss Universe  pageant is pretty similar to zaps but at  least he said the name of some  actually in the competition Harvey at  first declared miss Colombia the winner  and the pageant before realizing that he  misread the card he was forced to fix  his error and give the crown to Miss  Philippines but not until Miss Colombia  had a brief moment to celebrate the  mix-up caused a lot of mixed emotions  for the contestants and the audience and  made Steve Harvey a major newsworthy  topic and while you can say that zaps  mistake was a bit more foolish Harvey's  mistake was probably worse because he  had to disappoint someone who actually  was in the competition an underground  Kentucky Fried Chicken market seems like  it would never happen right well think  again because South Park actually got  this woman right while the idea is  pretty outrageous and is probably the  craziest on our list South Park  accurately predicted the existence of a  secret fried chicken market in 2010  during their medicinal fried chicken  episode the episode was originally based  on a KFC that was replaced in LA leading  to a bunch of outraged residents who  wanted their chicken back when this  event happened in South Park residents  went to extreme measures to make sure  they could get their fried chicken fix  Carmen developed a lucrative black  market where buckets of fried chicken  could be sold secretly to residents in  need of the fried food eight years later  this nightmare would become a reality in  the UK when 75% of KFC locations closed  for a period of a few days due to  unforeseen operational issues people  were unable to wait for the reopening  and began to buy buckets of KFC on eBay  that were being sold for as much as $100  each we don't even think South Park  realized how accurate this crazy idea  could be if a huge KFC shortage were to  actually occur South Park got another  prediction mostly right in 2008 in an  episode titled Brittany's a new look a  news anchor guessed that Miley Cyrus  would be pops next big megastar but he  also guessed that she would be the next  star to go off the rails similar to  Britney Spears 2007 meltdown hearing  this the people of South Park decide  that Miley Cyrus is their next big  obsession in 2008 Miley was only 16 and  still starring in the hit Disney Channel  series Hannah Montana but after the show  wrapped production Miley's creative  ventures took a turn that had people  questioning whether or not she was  headed for a downward spiral  first there was a revealing magazine  cover shoot the pole dance of the VMAs  and then her rebellious phase during the  early 2010's  with the release of party songs like we  can't stop from her bangers album  Miley even admitted that achieving  at such a young age you made her feel  like she had to find herself and rebell  a little bit but rebelling bought her  more into the public eye than ever  before  so while Miley didn't have a straight-up  meltdown and a career is still doing  pretty well South Park definitely  predicted her rise to super stardom and  the bad public behavior that came along  with it so while the things that these  cartoons predict may not be completely  accurate a hundred percent of the time  we have to admit that there have been  some pretty close calls in terms of  showrunners guessing what will happen in  the future  what prediction impressed you the most  and what are some other predictions  you've noticed in your favorite cartoons  let us know in the comments thanks for  watching don't forget to hit that like  button and subscribe to things for more  great content  [Music]  [Music]
 

